WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:23.425
When Nina arrived at summer camp, Mr. Dunn was setting a basket of lemons on the picnic table.

2
00:00:23.426 --> 00:00:26.673
"Good morning, Mr. Dunn!" she called.

3
00:00:26.674 --> 00:00:30.659
"Good morning, Nina," Mr. Dunn said.

4
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.773
Nina picked three lemons out of the basket.

5
00:00:35.774 --> 00:00:41.495
Her aunt had tried to teach her how to juggle last week.

6
00:00:41.496 --> 00:00:43.954
But Nina still couldn't do it.

7
00:00:43.955 --> 00:00:46.587
Plop, plop, plop.

8
00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:49.236
The lemons landed on the ground.

9
00:00:49.237 --> 00:00:54.858
By now the other campers arrived.

10
00:00:54.859 --> 00:00:58.658
"Hey, Nina!" Bobby laughed.

11
00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:01.738
"Did you sign up for clown school?"

12
00:01:01.739 --> 00:01:03.726
Nina frowned at him.

13
00:01:03.727 --> 00:01:05.851
"I'm not a clown!"

14
00:01:05.852 --> 00:01:08.132
Izzie picked up the lemons.

15
00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:11.291
"Do we need these lemons today?"

16
00:01:11.292 --> 00:01:16.017
Mr. Dunn nodded. "It's okay that they fell.

17
00:01:16.018 --> 00:01:20.152
We're going to squeeze all of the juice out of them anyway."

18
00:01:20.153 --> 00:01:27.797
"Yay! We're making lemonade!" Izzie cried.

19
00:01:27.798 --> 00:01:31.888
Inside the gym the kids gathered around Mr. Dunn.

20
00:01:31.889 --> 00:01:37.280
"Lemonade is one of my favorite summer drinks," the teacher said.

21
00:01:37.281 --> 00:01:40.407
"It's one of mine too!" said Izzie.

22
00:01:40.408 --> 00:01:43.217
"I like it really sweet."

23
00:01:43.218 --> 00:01:48.038
"Then you'll love this recipe," Mr. Dunn said.

24
00:01:48.039 --> 00:01:50.243
Ethan read the board.

25
00:01:50.244 --> 00:01:56.033
"To make the syrup, we have to heat the sugar and water until the sugar dissolves.

26
00:01:56.034 --> 00:01:59.054
But how will we know when the sugar dissolves?"

27
00:01:59.055 --> 00:02:06.734
"It'll disappear," said Mr. Dunn. "And turn into a clear syrup."

28
00:02:06.735 --> 00:02:14.272
Ethan and Jason made the syrup.

29
00:02:14.273 --> 00:02:16.933
The other campers cut lemons.

30
00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:20.655
Mr. Dunn handed forks to the lemon-cutters.

31
00:02:20.656 --> 00:02:23.988
"Now we remove the seeds."

32
00:02:23.989 --> 00:02:32.990
After Nina, Izzie, and Bobby removed the seeds, they squeezed the lemons to make juice.

33
00:02:32.991 --> 00:02:36.782
"Should we take out the pulp?" Nina asked.

34
00:02:36.783 --> 00:02:46.088
"No way!" Izzie cried. "Pulpy lemonade is the best!"

35
00:02:46.089 --> 00:02:51.483
Soon the syrup was cool, and the lemon juice was ready.

36
00:02:51.484 --> 00:02:57.089
Bobby poured them both into the pitcher.

37
00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:59.926
"Is that it?" he asked.

38
00:02:59.927 --> 00:03:02.910
"Almost," Mr. Dunn said.

39
00:03:02.911 --> 00:03:05.239
"We made the sweet part.

40
00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:08.079
And we made the sour part.

41
00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.419
Now we have to add water."

42
00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.555
"How much water?" Nina asked.

43
00:03:14.556 --> 00:03:18.218
"Let's start by adding two and half cups.

44
00:03:18.219 --> 00:03:24.073
We'll keep tasting the lemonade until it's just right," Mr. Dunn said.

45
00:03:24.074 --> 00:03:33.415
They each poured half a cup of water into the pitcher.

46
00:03:33.416 --> 00:03:38.104
Izzie poured herself a little lemonade.

47
00:03:38.105 --> 00:03:40.762
"Mmm. It's sweet!"

48
00:03:40.763 --> 00:03:43.193
Nina tried a small sip.

49
00:03:43.194 --> 00:03:45.139
"It's too sweet!

50
00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:48.015
Let's add more water."

51
00:03:48.016 --> 00:03:53.607
After they added one more half cup of water, Bobby tried the lemonade.

52
00:03:53.608 --> 00:03:57.203
"Mmm! That's good."

53
00:03:57.204 --> 00:03:59.657
Ethan tasted some too.

54
00:03:59.658 --> 00:04:01.816
"I think it needs more water.

55
00:04:01.817 --> 00:04:03.685
But only a little bit."

56
00:04:03.686 --> 00:04:06.782
"I agree," said Jason.

57
00:04:06.783 --> 00:04:11.321
"Let's just add ice cubes now," Nina suggested.

58
00:04:11.322 --> 00:04:14.664
"Great idea!" said Mr. Dunn.

59
00:04:14.665 --> 00:04:23.882
"Ice will cool the lemonade and add just a tiny bit of water."

60
00:04:23.883 --> 00:04:30.822
He got ice cubes from a cooler and added them to the pitcher.

61
00:04:30.823 --> 00:04:34.873
Then everyone had a glass of iced lemonade.

62
00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:40.494
"Wow! This is better than the lemonade at the deli," Izzie said.

63
00:04:40.495 --> 00:04:44.244
"This is good enough to sell!" Bobby said.

64
00:04:44.245 --> 00:04:50.108
"We could have a Kids Central Lemonade Stand!" Nina cried.

65
00:04:50.109 --> 00:04:59.894
"Then instead of juggling lemons, I can make lemonade!"
